<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ganimi Kava</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ganimi Kava is the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marathi">Marathi</a> term for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> tactics associated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha Empire</a>. Using light cavalry, rapid raids, ambushes and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hill-fort">hill forts</a>, the Marathas avoided pitched battles with larger armies such as those of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> and wore them down.</p></div>
